<title>CANADA: Canada government cash balances rise in week.</title>
<headline>Canada government cash balances rise in week.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The government of Canada's cash balances rose in the week that ended September 4, the Bank of Canada said on Friday.</p>
<p>				    Wk to Sept 4  Chg on wk Chg on yr</p>
<p>Notes in circulation		  27.69   +0.341    +0.356</p>
<p>Government cash balances	     6.81   +3.272    -1.409</p>
<p>Govt securities outstanding	467.49   +3.759   +10.422</p>
<p>Treasury bills			 153.90   +1.100   -12.400</p>
<p>Canada savings bonds		  30.08   -0.039    +0.635</p>
<p>All figures in billions of dollars.  </p>
<p>Chartered bank assets			   July	  June</p>
<p>   Net foreign currency			-12.63	-12.08</p>
<p>   Canadian dollar			     639.55	639.38</p>
<p>   Total Canadian liquid assets	    107.83	107.24</p>
<p>					 July 96    June 96     July 95</p>
<p>M1					 63.02	62.83	57.50</p>
<p>M2					389.79     391.32     381.65</p>
<p>M3					482.13     480.72     461.42</p>
<p>Note - Figures are unadjusted, in billions of dollars.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Ottawa Bureau (613) 235-6745</p>
</text>
